hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16021","Ishaq ibn Isa ibn al-Tabba narrated to us, he said, Jarir, meaning Ibn Hazim, narrated to us, from Wasil al-Ahdab, from Abu Wail, from Shurayh, he said, I heard a man of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, Allah, exalted, said: O son of Adam, stand to Me, I walk to you, and walk to Me, I hasten to you."
"16511","He said: Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shubah narrated to us, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban narrating from a man of the Ansar, from a man of the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Three are a duty upon every Muslim: ghusl on Friday, the siwak, and touching perfume if he finds it."
"16512","Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Sufyan, from Sad ibn Ibrahim, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Thawban, from a man of the Ansar, of the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: It is a duty upon every Muslim to wash on Friday, to use the siwak, and to touch perfume if his family has it."
"20619","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar narrated to us, from Budayl al-Uqayli, Abd Allah ibn Shaqiq informed me that one who heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed him, while he was at Wadi al-Qura on his horse, a man from Bulqin asked him and said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who are these? He said: These are those who earned anger, and he pointed to the Jews. He said: Who are these? He said: These are the astray, meaning the Christians."
"20620","He said: And a man came to him and said: Your freedman, or he said: your boy, so-and-so has been martyred. He said: Rather he is being dragged into the Fire in an aba cloak he stole."
"20802","Rawh narrated to us, Awf narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Abdullah al-Muzani, he said: A man narrated to me, he said: I was in a gathering in which Umar ibn al-Khattab was, in Madinah, and Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said to a man among those sitting with him: How did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say? He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Islam began as a jadha, then a thani, then a raba'i, then a sudasi, then a bazil. He said: So Umar said: There is nothing after full maturity except deficiency."
